    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do you convert Fahrenheit to Celsius?</h3>
        <p>Subtract 32, then multiply by 5/9. Formula: °C = (°F - 32) × 5/9. Example: 98.6°F = (98.6 - 32) × 5/9 = 37°C.</p>
      </div>
